style suggestion: do not rely on the DO variable 'd' after the loop
  --> tests/../integration_tests/gpu_residue_unroll_01.f90:55:37
   |
55 |                     final = final + d
   |                                     ^ after the loop, 'd' is one step past the last iteration
   |
51 |                     do d = (g-1)*8+1, g*8
   |                        ~ the loop sets 'd' here
   = help: the value is well defined, but it depends on how the loop ends and
           is easy to misread; inside the loop, assign the value you need to
           a variable with a meaningful name instead
